# Brief pipeline queue files. Generated by the cron jobs nightly.
# Excluded from git: these are operational state, not source.
# The audit-log/ subdirectory is also generated; ops can opt to commit it
# if a long-term audit trail in git is desired.

*-ingested.json
*-audited.json
*-decisions.json
audit-log/*.json

# Output of brief-prep.ts. Holds the FULL TEXT of other newsrooms' articles,
# fetched so the firewall can verify drafted claims against them. It is working
# evidence for one day's run, not source, and must never be committed.
*-prepared.json

# Keep this gitignore tracked so the directory exists.
!.gitignore

# Research packets hold the FULL TEXT of other outlets' articles, fetched so the
# firewall can verify a feature against them. Working evidence for one piece,
# not source. topics.json IS tracked: it is the editorial record of what has
# been researched, published and dropped.
articles/*.json
!articles/topics.json
